│     • Location 1: File: sphinx/ext/autodoc.py, Class: autodoc,     │
│       Method: visit_method                                         │
│       Intended Behavior: The visit_method method should add the    │
│       method to the index without parentheses, as it is a method,  │
│       not a property.                                              │
│     • Location 2: File: sphinx/ext/autodoc.py, Class: autodoc,     │
│       Method: process                                              │
│       Intended Behavior: The process method should ensure that the │
│       :property: option is handled correctly, preserving the       │
│       method's index entry without parentheses.                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Explanation:                                                       │
│ The py:method:: directive with :property: is being misprocessed    │
│ because the autodoc module's visit_method and process methods are  │
│ adding parentheses to the index entry. The intended behavior is to │
│ treat :property: as a property directive, not a method, so the     │
│ index entry should not include parentheses. The fix involves       │
│ modifying these methods to avoid adding parentheses when the       │
│ :property: option is present.                                      │
